# Section 4: The Development of AI Technology

## 4.1 From Rule-Based Systems to Modern AI

📘 A **rule-based (expert) system** stores knowledge as "if–then" rules written by experts. These are transparent but hard to scale. Modern AI instead learns patterns from large datasets.

## 4.2 Technologies Behind AI Development

| Ingredient | Role |
|---|---|
| **Big data** | Large amounts of examples to learn from |
| **Computing hardware (GPUs/TPUs)** | Fast number processing for training large models |
| **Better algorithms** | Backpropagation, convolutional networks, transformers |
| **Open software and research sharing** | Faster progress and reuse |

## 4.3 How AI Capabilities Have Expanded

AI moved from narrow rules (playing checkers) → statistical learning (spam filters) → perception (image and speech recognition) → language and content generation. Each step was enabled by more data, more computing power, and improved methods.

