# Section 7: AI in Everyday Life

## 7.1 AI in Language Translation
Neural machine translation models learn from large collections of paired texts in two languages, translating whole sentences in context rather than word by word. Quality varies by language and topic, and idioms or specialized terms may be mistranslated.

## 7.2 AI in Education
Uses include personalized practice, automated feedback, tutoring assistants, and accessibility tools (captions, text-to-speech). Cautions: accuracy of generated explanations, student data privacy, and the risk of over-reliance.

## 7.3 AI in Recommendation Systems
📘 A **recommendation system** predicts what a user may like based on past behavior and similar users. Streaming and shopping services use these. Risk: **filter bubbles** that narrow what people see.

## 7.4 AI in Healthcare
Examples: analyzing medical images, predicting protein structures (Jumper et al., 2021), and drafting clinical notes. Such tools are meant to **support**, not replace, clinicians, and they require careful testing and regulation.

## 7.5 AI in Virtual Assistants
Voice assistants convert speech to text, work out intent, perform an action, and respond using synthesized speech. They can mishear accents, background noise, or unusual requests.

