# Section 8: AI-Powered Research and Search Engines

## 8.1 How AI Improves Information Retrieval
Traditional search matches keywords. AI-based retrieval can match *meaning* (semantic search) by converting text into numbers called 📘 **embeddings** so that similar ideas lie close together.

## 8.2 AI-Powered Search Engines
Modern systems may combine search with an LLM that summarizes results, a method often called 📘 **retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)**. The system retrieves relevant documents first, then writes an answer based on them (Lewis et al., 2020).

## 8.3 AI in Scientific Research and Data Analysis
AI helps scan literature, find patterns in large datasets, and accelerate discovery, such as predicting protein structures (Jumper et al., 2021).

## 8.4 Benefits and Limitations of AI Research Tools

| Benefits | Limitations |
|---|---|
| Faster literature review | May invent or misquote sources |
| Finds hidden patterns | Can reflect biases in source material |
| Summarizes long documents | Summaries may omit key nuance |

**Good practice:** always open and verify the cited source.

