# Section 10: AI in Weather Forecasting and Climate Analysis

## 10.1 How AI Predicts Weather Changes
Weather depends on temperature, pressure, humidity, and wind. Traditional forecasting uses physics-based equations (numerical weather prediction). AI models learn patterns from decades of recorded weather data to predict future conditions.

## 10.2 Machine Learning in Weather Forecasting
Models such as GraphCast learn from historical reanalysis data and produce global forecasts quickly, with accuracy competitive with leading traditional systems on many measures (Lam et al., 2023).

## 10.3 AI for Climate Change Analysis
Climate is long-term weather patterns. AI supports analyzing satellite imagery, tracking ice and forests, and improving climate model components.

## 10.4 Benefits and Limitations of AI Weather Predictions

| Benefits | Limitations |
|---|---|
| Very fast once trained | Depends on quality of historical data |
| Lower computing cost per forecast | May struggle with rare extreme events not seen in training |
| Can complement physics-based models | Less transparent about *why* a forecast is made |

